<title>SINGAPORE: Shell Singapore restarted hydrocracker on Sunday.</title>
<headline>Shell Singapore restarted hydrocracker on Sunday.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell Singapore restarted its 4,900 tonnes-per-day (36,750 barrels per day) hydrocracker late Sunday, a company spokeswoman said on Monday.</p>
<p>She said the hydrocracker, which was closed December 17 due to boiler leakage, was in the process of being started-up and was running at almost 100 percent.</p>
<p>The unit is located at Shell's 435,000 barrel-per-day refinery at Pulau Bukom, off Singapore's south coast.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
